      "claim": "In male NMRI mice, [18F]-5 showed negligible brain uptake at 2 and 60 minutes, providing a contradictory low-similarity example of poor CNS access.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "moderate",
  "decision_summary": "Multiple structurally similar analogs with direct in vivo data demonstrate meaningful BBB penetration and CNS exposure after systemic administration. The single negative analog is less similar and outweighed by the positive evidence, so the query is predicted to have meaningful CNS access.",
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct query-specific CNS exposure data are available; prediction relies on structurally similar analogs with moderate Morgan similarity.",
    "One low-similarity analog showed negligible brain uptake, leaving some uncertainty about whether the query could share that liability.",
    "Some positive records involve PET tracers or transporter-mediated uptake, which may not fully represent passive CNS access for the query."
  ],
